{
  "_comment": [
    "THE ONLY PLACE A FRAME SIZE LIVES (docs/ship-kit.md). Every screen a demo is filmed on, every canvas it is",
    "composed into and every App Store slot it is exported for. scripts/gen_devices.py emits",
    "capture/demo/devices.py (standard library, the Mac's capture), mobile/src/generated/devices.ts and",
    "Packages/BuilderKit/Sources/BuilderModel/Generated/Devices.swift. Never hand-edit the output.",
    "",
    "WHY A TABLE. Another demo tool drew an iPhone that came out elongated: a capture at one size",
    "composed into a frame of another, stretched to fit. Here the capture chooses a row, the run is",
    "REFUSED when the pixels it recorded are not that row's pixels within `match_tolerance`, and the",
    "composer draws the row's own shape at its own aspect, so a stretched phone cannot be made.",
    "",
    "WHERE EACH NUMBER COMES FROM. Every row with `simulator_types` was MEASURED on this Mac, from iOS",
    "itself, by scripts/measure_devices.py (UIScreen.bounds, scale and nativeBounds; the full screen",
    "view's safeAreaInsets in portrait; UIScreen._displayCornerRadius), on a fresh simulator of each type,",
    "with the device type's own profile.plist read beside it; the results are",
    "docs/research/device-measurements.json and `gen_devices.py --verify` holds this file to them. A row",
    "lists several simulator types only where every one of them measured the same. The Mac window rows",
    "cannot be measured in a simulator: their sizes are the default scaled resolutions of the Macs named,",
    "and their corner radius is a drawing choice, said so in `source`."
  ],
  "version": 1,
  "match_tolerance": 0.005,
  "_match_tolerance": "0.5%: a capture whose width or height differs from its row's pixels by more than this is refused. A 1206x2622 row accepts 1200 to 1212 by 2609 to 2635, which takes the one pixel a web page's rounding adds (MEASURED: two of the Personal Website's stills came out 1206x2623 and 1206x2621) and refuses every other iPhone in this table.",
