  "terminal": {
    "format": "vertical",
    "corner_radius": 40,
    "_why": "A CLI or a library has no device: VHS types into a terminal the size of the vertical format, so the reel needs no scaling at all, and the square, feed and landscape posts draw it as a card with this radius, in pixels of that canvas. A drawing choice, not a measurement."
  },
  "_same_screen": "Two rows may share one pixel size, and only exactly (the iPad Air 11-inch and the iPad (A16): 1640x2360, MEASURED corner radius 18 and 25). A capture is checked against the row it was filmed on, which it names; `devices.match_pixels`, used only for a demo made before the table, answers the first row listed.",
  "_native_scale": "`scale` is UIKit's (UIScreen.scale), `native_scale` the panel's (UIScreen.nativeScale). They differ on one row: MEASURED, the iPhone 13 and 12 mini lay out 375x812 points at 3x and the panel is 1080x2340, 2.88 pixels a point, so a screenshot is the panel's pixels and a table that multiplied points by scale would have expected 1125x2436, a phone 4% too tall."
}
